    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13595" root="دين" body-key="d">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَدِينَةٌ</span></b>  <i>A city;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِصْرٌ</span>: (S, K:) so called
because had, or held, in possession, or under
authority. (S, * TA.) [See also art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مدن</span>.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَنَا ٱبْنُ مَدِينَتِهَا</span> means <i>I am he who is acquainted
with it;</i> (IAar, T, * M, * K;) like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ابن بَجْدَتِهَا</span>
[q. v.]. (IAar, T.)

